{# `App\MessageHandler\SendEmailMessageHandler` renders this file the same
   three-block way verify_email.html.twig documents. Sent to the child's own
   newly-set real address (S2's `email_verified_at` stays null until they act,
   same as any other new account) once a parent enables sign-in
   (`ChildAccountService::enableSignIn()`, D1d). Context: `invitationUrl` (an
   absolute URL to the already-shipped `app_account_invitation` route, built
   by the handler from the message's raw `token`), `childName`. #}
{% if false %}
    {% block subject %}Set up your sign-in for the platform{% endblock %}
    {% block text %}
Hello {{ childName }},

A parent has enabled sign-in for your player account on the platform. Set
your password to activate it by opening the link below:

{{ invitationUrl }}

This link expires in 7 days. If you were not expecting this, you can safely
ignore this email.
    {% endblock %}
{% endif %}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <meta charset="UTF-8">
        <title>{{ block('subject') }}</title>
    </head>
    <body>
        <p>Hello {{ childName }},</p>
        <p>A parent has enabled sign-in for your player account on the platform. Set your password to activate it by clicking the link below:</p>
        <p><a href="{{ invitationUrl }}">Set your password</a></p>
        <p>This link expires in 7 days. If you were not expecting this, you can safely ignore this email.</p>
    </body>
</html>
